mderi_block  @968a8638
  why   Every integral of one shell quartet: the unit of work of the build and
        of the Schwarz bound. Written as two matrix products, the sums over
        primitives run inside `@`, and one Boys evaluation and one R table per
        primitive quartet serve every component
        [test "all 18145 water 6-31G* ERIs match PySCF to 1e-12"].
  ST    the store
  k1    the bra pair's index in the store
  k2    the ket pair's index
  G     the Boys grid from mderi_grid
  o1    where the bra's pack starts; o2 the ket's
  L1    the bra's total angular momentum; L2 the ket's
  np1   the bra's primitive pairs; np2 the ket's
  nh1   the bra's Hermite functions; nh2 the ket's
  L     the quartet's total angular momentum
  D     the side of the R cube
  HA    the R offsets of the bra's Hermite functions; HC the ket's
  SG    the ket's signs $(-1)^{t'+u'+v'}$
  ncd   the ket's component pairs
  E2    the ket's $E_{cd}$ as a matrix
  nbat  how many bra primitive pairs one batch holds, so BR stays near
        `MDERI_BATCH` entries
  BR    the signed R values of one batch: a row per ket (primitive pair,
        Hermite function), a column per bra one
  ZT    $Z^\top$  every batch's $E_{cd}\,BR$, transposed and stacked
  S     the R cube buffer for herm_rfill
  F     the Boys values
  c52   $2\pi^{5/2}$, the constant of the ERI formula
  k0    the first bra primitive pair of the batch
  kn    the batch's size, smaller at the end
  b1    where the bra primitive pair's $(p, P)$ sits; b2 the ket's
  p     the bra pair's exponent; q the ket's
  X     $P - Q$ on $x$; Y and Z likewise
  al    $\alpha = pq/(p+q)$, the exponent of the Boys argument
  row   the row of BR for this ket primitive pair and Hermite function
  base  the R offset of this ket Hermite function
  sg    its sign
  Zb    one batch's $E_{cd}\,BR$

  $$ (ab|cd) = \frac{2\pi^{5/2}}{pq\sqrt{p+q}} \sum_{h} E_{ab}(h) \sum_{h'} (-1)^{t'+u'+v'} E_{cd}(h')\, R(h + h') $$  [test "all 18145 water 6-31G* ERIs match PySCF to 1e-12"]
  = nbat  batches keep BR small whatever the contraction depth
  = al    the exponent of the Boys argument; herm_boys_fill and herm_rfill then build this primitive quartet's R table, with the ERI constant folded in
  = BR#2  the signed R entry for one ket and one bra Hermite function
  = Zb    the ket's sums, over its primitives and Hermite functions, as one product
  = ZT#2  this batch's rows of $Z^\top$

